    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p63-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the length of the radius of the circle, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$92.19\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "Bisect one of the seven equal central triangles. Its half-angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{7}$, and its half-base is $40\\text{ cm}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}s &= \\frac{560}{7}\\text{ cm}\\\\s &= 80\\text{ cm}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{7} &= \\frac{40}{r}\\\\r &= \\frac{40}{\\sin(\\pi/7)}\\text{ cm}\\\\r &\\approx 92.19\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p63-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the total area of the shaded parts, correct to the nearest square centimetre.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p63-q23-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "3444\\text{ cm}^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p63-q23-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Subtract the seven central triangle areas from the circle area, using the unrounded radius.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Each central angle is $\\frac{2\\pi}{7}$. Use the unrounded radius from part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A &= \\pi r^2-7\\left(\\frac12r^2\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{7}\\right)\\\\A &= r^2\\left(\\pi-\\frac72\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{7}\\right)\\\\A &= \\left(\\frac{40}{\\sin(\\pi/7)}\\right)^2\\left(\\pi-\\frac72\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{7}\\right)\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A &\\approx 3444\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe total shaded area is $3444\\text{ cm}^2$, to the nearest square centimetre.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
